This is a fantasy-world game that fulfills all my dreams. Even though it lacks depth in equipment and build — and the expansion to six skill slots doesn't offer much variety —the stat bonuses from leveling up (dragon dogma 1) still manage to create meaningful differences between characters in new playthroughs even it was also a terrible idea. In Dragon's Dogma 2, however, characters lack this kind of differentiation, which is a real shame given the excellent character creation system. And I liked to see  other players pawn hang out of the town. some times i attack them because goblin is more cute.  I’ve been waiting a long time for DLC; I know there will likely only be one expansion, but if you want my money, here is what I’d suggest: 
DLC 2—Secrets of the Elven Tree (new enchantment and equipment system, shot lingerie is acceptable too haha); 
DLC 3—Dwarven Treasure (dungeons in the volcanic region); 
and DLC 4—A Happy Life for Me and my main pawn (housing system expansion). I have to say, while you can buy a house in the base game, it’s essentially like putting money in a bank—aside from saving some cash, it serves no actual purpose. 
Finally Capcom is like a child who could have earned an A+ but settled for a B, simply because a B was enough to get a reward.
